# Big raw downloads — keep these out of the repo
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
# ...EXCEPT the IMD scores CSV, which is small and must persist so every
# cloud build can see it (this fixes the recurring "sample data" problem).
!data/raw/imd2025_scores.csv

# Station locations CSV for the rail overlay — same reasoning: small, must
# persist so the cloud build can read it (drag-and-drop can't upload dotfiles,
# but a normal CSV via "Add file" works fine).
!data/raw/uk_stations.csv

# ORR "Estimates of station usage". Commit the CSV(s) you download from the ORR
# data portal here. Table 1410 (single year) carries the rich fields
# (interchanges, ticket split, region, quality); Table 1415 (time series) adds
# the multi-year trend. Commit 1410 as the primary; optionally add 1415 too and
# the builder merges the trend. Several accepted names:
!data/raw/orr_station_usage.csv
!data/raw/orr_station_usage_1410.csv
!data/raw/orr_station_usage_1415.csv
!data/raw/orr_1410.csv
!data/raw/orr_1415.csv
!data/raw/orr_station_usage_timeseries.csv

# Brownfield Land Register national download (planning.data.gov.uk). Build
# input for build_brownfield_csv.py -> supabase/brownfield_import.csv. Larger
# (~tens of MB) but git handles it; it's a build input, not published to Pages.
!data/raw/brownfield-land.csv
!data/raw/brownfield-land.json
!data/raw/brownfield-land.geojson

# Optional GP practice file fallback: if the NHS auto-download is blocked, you
# can download the CSV in your browser and commit it here, and the loader will
# use it instead of downloading. Small, so safe to keep in the repo.
!data/raw/epraccur.csv

# LSOA 2021 boundary file downloaded from the ONS Open Geography portal (BGC,
# 20m). Committing it lets the build use it directly instead of the flaky ONS
# API. It's larger (~tens of MB) but git handles it and the deploy strips it.
!data/raw/lsoa_2021_bgc.geojson

# Planning-constraint source downloads (build inputs for build_constraints.py ->
# supabase/constraints_import.csv). They're clipped to a 1 km buffer around every
# rail station, so the DB stays tiny, but the raw national files are large. Commit
# whichever you have (or fetch them in CI). Filenames are the build's defaults;
# override with the *_SRC env vars if yours differ.
!data/raw/os_open_built_up_areas.gpkg
!data/raw/os_open_built_up_areas.shp
!data/raw/os_open_greenspace.gpkg
!data/raw/os_open_greenspace.shp
!data/raw/os_openmap_local.gpkg
!data/raw/ea_flood_zone_2.gpkg
!data/raw/ea_flood_zone_3.gpkg
!data/raw/ea_flood_zones.gpkg
!data/raw/green-belt.geojson
!data/raw/green_belt.geojson

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: web/data/lsoa_imd.geojson is intentionally NOT ignored —
# GitHub Pages must serve it. The Action commits it for you.

# Supabase loaders: large optional postcode-centroid lookup (download locally;
# the loader also falls back to the postcodes.io API if this is absent).
data/raw/postcodes.csvnode_modules/
node_modules/

# NPPF well-connected: connectivity + TTWA-GVA build inputs/outputs (small, kept for reproducibility)
!data/raw/station_connectivity.csv
!data/raw/ttwa_top60.csv
!data/raw/ttwa_2011.geojson
!data/raw/ttwa_gva.xlsx
